# review: the branch an agent pushed, read as its merge request shows it. --review=agent/refund
# fetches it from the local origin and opens on the first hunk; the panel marks each file M, A or
# D with its +n −m. c / C walk the hunks across files: the imports three lines apart are two hunks
# though the fixture sets diff.interHunkContext (#220), the redrawn PNG is skipped (#77), the
# deleted script opens read-only. The lines the branch deleted at the end of repos.py are lines
# the cursor walks down to the last one (#179, #439), painted as deletions (#144, #165). d from a
# changed line into the function the branch added, [ back to the hunk; m puts the tick on the open
# file and takes it off (#162). Last, c after a d into a file the branch did not touch goes back into the review,
# to the hunk left once #239 lands (0.7.0 opens the first file). On such a file the status bar has no
# counters, as outside a review (#286). Back in repos.py, c stands on the first line the branch
# deleted and the status bar reads its old number, negative; / finds the deleted text, Ctrl+C
# copies it, and an edit there is refused (#439). The panel's status letters are plain, in the
# row's style (#450). o lists the review's files first, each with its panel letter, and u marks
# the uses on lines the branch changed with the gutter's bar (#246). Then `merl -r agent/page-size`
# from the main checkout: the branch an agent has checked out in a worktree of its own is reviewed
# there, its file not committed yet included (#396). Back on agent/refund, d on a line the
# branch deleted reads its word there and lands on the deleted field it names, [ back (#440).
# Then p on that worktree's Markdown file renders it, p again shows its source (#596). Last,
# `merl -r agent/totp` reviews a Java package eleven directories deep: the panel folds its
# one-child chain into `…/twofactor/totp`, so both file names fit (#399).
caption review · merl --review=agent/refund fetches the agent's branch and opens on its first hunk
merl --review=agent/refund
wait hunk 1/1  file 1/8
caption c: the next hunk, across files; the panel marks each file M, A or D with its +n −m
key c
wait hunk 1/1  file 2/8
caption the lines the branch deleted at the end of repos.py are lines: PgDn walks them, down to the last (#179, #439)
key PageDown
wait self.orders.clear()
caption two imports three lines apart are two hunks, though git's interHunkContext would merge them (#220)
key c
wait hunk 1/4  file 3/8
key c
wait hunk 2/4  file 3/8
key c c
wait hunk 4/4  file 3/8
